  "id": "COMPOUND:32025 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between (2E)-3-(7-methoxy-2H-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol and the serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. This compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Itaconic Anhydride and RA-Xii, both of which are known to interact with EDD domain proteins in the DegV family. These EDD domain proteins are ultimately targeted by CDC2L1, indicating a potential pathway where the compound may modulate the activity of CDC2L1 through interaction with its target. The consistent presence of EDD domain proteins as intermediaries across the three paths supports a model where the compound exerts its effect via a common mechanism, possibly involving binding to EDD domain proteins and subsequent modulation of CDC2L1 activity. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological roles of EDD domain proteins in cellular processes, making the proposed relationship a plausible candidate for further investigation.",
